## 5.2 The OpenFileDialog and SaveFileDialog Controls

- They display the standard Windows **Open** and **Save As** dialog boxes
- They are *invisible controls*: they appear in the **component tray** at the bottom of the Designer, not on the form

### Showing an Open dialog

```csharp
private void openButton_Click(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    openFileDialog.ShowDialog();
}
```
### Detecting the user's choice

`ShowDialog` returns a `DialogResult`:

- `DialogResult.OK`: user clicked Open (or Save)
- `DialogResult.Cancel`: user clicked Cancel

```csharp
DialogResult result = openFileDialog.ShowDialog();
if (result == DialogResult.OK)
{
    // use the file
}
else if (result == DialogResult.Cancel)
{
    // user cancelled
}
```
### FileName and InitialDirectory

- `FileName`: holds the path and name of the file the user selected
- `InitialDirectory`: the folder shown first when the dialog opens

```csharp
openFileDialog.InitialDirectory = @"C:\Data";

if (openFileDialog.ShowDialog() == DialogResult.OK)
{
    inputFile = File.OpenText(openFileDialog.FileName);
}
```
### Save As dialog

```csharp
if (saveFileDialog.ShowDialog() == DialogResult.OK)
{
    outputFile = File.CreateText(saveFileDialog.FileName);
}
```
